        "id": "na7BL4JSWsq-"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Answer 4:**\n",
        "KNN works by measuring distances between customers, so a feature with large values (like `TotalCharges`, in the thousands) would dominate features with small values (like 0/1 dummy columns, or tenure in months), and the \"nearest\" neighbours would be decided almost entirely by the biggest-scale features. Logistic Regression is trained with gradient-based optimisation and its coefficients are only comparable across features when they share a scale. Decision Trees and Random Forests only ask \"is this feature above or below a threshold?\", so changing a feature's scale does not change where the best split is, and no scaling is needed."
      ],
      "id": "na7BL4JSWsq-"
    },
    {
